# The shape of the control host's js-server command line: the arguments its stack gives the
# js-lease-server image, one a line, in the same order, with the same kinds of value. The
# control host runs the image as uid and gid 65532, with a read-only root file system, every
# capability dropped, a tmpfs at /tmp, its secrets under /run/secrets and its configuration files
# under /etc/js-lease-server; the black-box test starts the container the same way. What
# differs is the network: the control host listens on all addresses of an overlay network behind
# a proxy, and the test listens on this host's loopback (Docker's host network), on ports it
# picks (the placeholders). The store is a Postgres database there and here.
#
# When the control host's command line gains, loses or changes an argument, change this file in
# the same way.
--listen
127.0.0.1:{agent_port}
--job-listen
127.0.0.1:{job_port}
--ready-listen
127.0.0.1:{ready_port}
--metrics-listen
127.0.0.1:{metrics_port}
--tls-cert
/etc/js-lease-server/tls.pem
--tls-key
/run/secrets/tls.key
--state-file
/var/lib/js-lease-server/leases.toml
--boot
resume
--token-file
/run/secrets/token
--agent-pool-config
/etc/js-lease-server/pool.toml
--agent-pool-config
/etc/js-lease-server/pool-mac-build.toml
--agent-token-file
/run/secrets/join-tokens
--agent-client-ca
/etc/js-lease-server/agent-client-ca.pem
--store
/run/secrets/store.url
--client-token
kbf=/run/secrets/kbf-client-token
--cold-cpu-millis
4000
--cold-memory-bytes
17179869184
--cold-cpu-millis-on
macos=1500
--cold-memory-bytes-on
macos=6442450944
--tick
1s
--placement-curves
shadow
